==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|gobbledegook}}; [[gobblygook]], [[garbley gook]], [[gobbly-gook]]

===Etymology===
First attested in a memo by US Representative (Texas) {{w|Maury Maverick}} dated March 30, 1944, banning "gobbledygook language". Apparently coined in imitation of the sounds made by a turkey.

Mr. Maury Maverick was, incidentally, the grandson of lawyer and politician {{w|Samuel Maverick}}, whose behaviour regarding his cattle inspired the term ''[[maverick]]'' ("offbeat").

